## The key architectural rule

If I had to reduce all of this to **one rule for EKS**, it would be:

> **No programming language implementation is allowed to become the semantic authority for EKS.**

The semantic authority must be the **language-independent contract + domain invariants + conformance oracle**.

That is the architectural mechanism that lets you have PHP today, Python tomorrow, Rust later, or several languages simultaneously **without changing what EKS means**.

And importantly, this is exactly why I would finish the current `KOS-CONTRACT-NEUTRALITY-001` reconciliation **before introducing another language implementation**. The existing LCOM4 history has already shown that the hardest problem is not translating PHP to Python; it is making sure the contract itself is precise enough that two independent implementations can reach the same answer.
